_pdbx_database_remark.id     650 
_pdbx_database_remark.text   
;HELIX
EACH HELIX IS LABELED BY TWO DIGITS.  THE FIRST INDICATES
THE DOMAIN WHERE THE HELIX IS LOCATED AND THE SECOND GIVES
ITS SEQUENTIAL NUMBER.  THE DIGITS ARE SEPARATED BY THE
CHAIN IDENTIFIER.  BECAUSE THE HELIX IDENTIFIERS ARE
RESTRICTED TO THREE CHARACTERS, HELIX 4-10 AND 4-11 OF BOTH
CHAINS ARE LABELED 4A1, 4AA, 4B1 AND 4BA.
;
# 
